    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d899">

                <pb facs="1074" n="1064" sameAs="frus:frus1943v01/pg1064"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.515/576b: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-04-05T13:00:00-04:00">April 5, 1943—1
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2124. From the Under Secretary. Secretary Morgenthau asked me to let you know, in
                    reply to your message<anchor n="28" xml:id="d899-f1"/> which he received this
                    morning, that in view of the publication he is having a press conference at 3
                    p.m. tomorrow, Tuesday, April 6, at which he will give the press the text of the
                    stabilization plan for release in the morning papers of April 7. [Welles.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d899-f1" n="28" xml:id="d899-f1-content">
